From: Will Buchta <buchtawill@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 23 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: ov9282: enable STROBE exposure-indicator output

The OV9281 STROBE pad (B6) is a "frame exposure output indicator" -- it pulses
in sync with the pixel-array integration window, ideal for gating a strobed IR
illuminator on the mocap rig. It is disabled at reset and by the vendor init:
common_regs writes 0x3006=0x04 (io_pad_out_en bit2 = ILPWM out; STROBE bit3 = 0
= input), and never sets 0x392F (reset 0x40) so r_strobe_frm_pwen (bit7) = 0,
leaving the strobe engine off.

Enable it by default in common_regs (applied every start_streaming, so both
free-run and external-trigger modes get it):
  - 0x3006: 0x04 -> 0x0C  (set bit3: STROBE pad = output; FSIN bit1 stays input,
    so external-trigger input is unaffected)
  - 0x392F: add 0xC0      (bit7 r_strobe_frm_pwen = 1, keep bit6 r_strobe_frm_pwst)

0x3027 bit3 (STROBE output select) is left at its reset 0 = normal data path, so
the strobe engine (not a static register value) drives the pin. Pulse polarity
(0x392F bit5 r_strobe_pol) and width/shift (0x3921-0x3928) keep their defaults;
tune on a scope for the specific illuminator.

Signed-off-by: Will Buchta <buchtawill@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov9282.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov9282.c
@@ -208,7 +208,7 @@
 	{0x3001, 0x00},
 	{0x3004, 0x00},
 	{0x3005, 0x00},
-	{0x3006, 0x04},
+	{0x3006, 0x0c},	/* io_pad_out_en: bit3 STROBE=output (was bit2 ILPWM only) */
 	{0x3011, 0x0a},
 	{0x3013, 0x18},
 	{0x301c, 0xf0},
@@ -247,6 +247,7 @@
 	{0x38c6, 0x04},
 	{0x38c7, 0x80},
 	{0x3920, 0xff},
+	{0x392f, 0xc0},	/* PWM_CTRL_2F: bit7 r_strobe_frm_pwen=1 (enable strobe engine) */
 	{0x4010, 0x40},
 	{0x4043, 0x40},
 	{0x4307, 0x30},
